# Helper Functions Standards

## tests/helpers/ Usage

- Put shared / cross-module helpers under `tests/helpers/`.
- Prefer named files by concern (e.g. `action-logger.ts`, `healer-mode.ts`, `*-ui-heal.ts`).
- Examples:
  - navigation helpers
  - common action methods
  - element visibility checks
  - module-specific heal / API mock helpers

Example:

```typescript
export async function navigateToPage(page: Page, baseUrl: string, path: string): Promise<void> {
  await page.goto(`${baseUrl}${path}`);
  await page.waitForLoadState("domcontentloaded");
}
```

## Rules

- Do not duplicate reusable logic in page objects.
- If used in more than 2 places → move into `tests/helpers/`.
- Helper functions must be generic and reusable (or scoped clearly to one module).
